      "writtenOn": "2022-05-27T12:45:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "For properties and attributes in Soong, using a pointer over a scalar allows us to distinguish between the unset value and an intentionally empty value. In this case, even if Output_extension is unset, we\u0027ll output `output_extension \u003d \"\"`",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 822,
        "startChar": 18,
        "endLine": 822,
        "endChar": 24
      },
      "revId": "468d5061e596a3d5d21344b059207f89228de396",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8f8048b4_c954f557",
        "filename": "genrule/genrule.go",
        "patchSetId": 13
      },
      "lineNbr": 822,
      "author": {
        "id": 1938760
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-05-27T18:43:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "[Here](https://android-review.git.corp.google.com/c/platform/external/boringssl/+/1970879/13/Android.bp#641) is one (only) example where `output_extension` is unset. In that scenario, the output file will be \"src/rust/src/lib.\" I confirmed this in the ninja action locally.\n\nSo while the extension being empty is rare, it\u0027s actually intact with how Soong works.\n\nMoving forward, I think we should let Soong errors if `output_extension` is empty. WDYT? If you agree, we can create a bug to address this separately.",
      "parentUuid": "c1c9ce98_2c4dde89",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 822,
        "startChar": 18,
        "endLine": 822,
        "endChar": 24
      },
      "revId": "468d5061e596a3d5d21344b059207f89228de396",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
