      "writtenOn": "2022-05-27T19:05:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "She\u0027s referring to this bit of code that I added a while ago to attach labels to modules generated at Soong runtime: https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:build/soong/android/hooks.go;l\u003d113;drc\u003d85468a34f119e699f604718701d2ff8721d3105c\n\nUsed here, for example: https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:build/soong/android/hooks.go;l\u003d135;drc\u003df31c90050cf47cc8a46aefb21beff628ef90ad9b.\n\nSo since we\u0027re doing `ctx.ModuleType() \u003d\u003d \"gensrcs` it would not match a module with type `gensrcs_loadHookModule` which might exist. Could do `strings.HasPrefix(ctx.ModuleType(), \"gensrcs\")` or do something similar to cc module where the type is determined via reflection: https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:build/soong/cc/cc.go;l\u003d3567;drc\u003d5bec8d41ea85cd409c4e914d3f0959a88b64277e.",
